```{r setup, message=FALSE, warning=FALSE}
library(tidyverse)
merged_data <- read_csv("data/processed/nys_merged.csv")
```

## County Summary

```{r}
summary_data <- merged_data |>
  group_by(county_name) |>
  summarise(
    total_enrollment = sum(total_enroll, na.rm = TRUE),
    lunch_percent = mean(
      per_free_lunch + per_reduced_lunch,
      na.rm = TRUE
    ) * 100,
    poverty_percent = mean(
      county_per_poverty,
      na.rm = TRUE
    ) * 100
  )

summary_data
```

## Poverty and Lunch Assistance

```{r}
summary_data |>
  ggplot(aes(poverty_percent, lunch_percent)) +
  geom_point(na.rm = TRUE) +
  labs(
    title = "Higher poverty is associated with more lunch assistance",
    x = "Poverty (%)",
    y = "Lunch assistance (%)"
  ) +
  theme_minimal()
```

Counties with higher poverty generally have more students receiving free or reduced-price lunch.
